{"id":"8345fef05678148a88e71f5c66959e2d25a20e89","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"8345fef05678148a88e71f5c66959e2d25a20e89","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/allow-build-writes-permissions.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"pacquet\": patch","+---","+","+`pnpm add --allow-build` now records its decision under `permissions` when `pnpm-workspace.yaml` has a `permissions` setting. Before, a `--allow-build=!<pkg>` denial went to `allowBuilds` and was overridden by an existing `permissions.<pkg>.build: true`."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":".changeset/approve-all-keeps-denials.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"pacquet\": patch","+---","+","+`pnpm approve-builds --all` and `pnpm approve --all` no longer approve a package whose build is denied with `false` in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":".changeset/named-registry-build-approvals.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"pacquet\": patch","+---","+","+A `<pkg>@<version>: false` entry in `allowBuilds` or `permissions` now also blocks `<pkg>@<version>` from a named registry, including when `dangerouslyAllowAllBuilds` is set."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":".changeset/permissions-flow-entry-refused.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"pacquet\": patch","+---","+","+`pnpm approve-builds`, `pnpm approve`, and `pnpm add --allow-build` now refuse to edit a package's `permissions` entry written as an inline mapping that spans several lines. Before, they added a second key for the package to `pnpm-workspace.yaml`."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/src/cli_args/approve_builds.rs","lines":["@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@ use prompt::{"," use std::{","     collections::{","         BTreeMap,","+        HashMap,","         HashSet,","     },","     path::Path,","@@ -162,9 +163,12 @@ impl ApproveBuildsArgs {","         config: &Config,","         rebuild_config: &Config,","  